  "Formulas D.9 (`event_due`, EVENT_SAVE_SETTLE_TICKS row L767); MSA-33 (d); MSA-39; AC-MSA-54 (L1749); T9; Dependencies S1(b)/(c); OQ 39/45; registry `last_shape_change_T` consumer copy (L5235): [main review, promoted by creative-director] Assembly and its owner disagree on what `event_due` computes. Assembly's D.9 still has the `(T - last_shape_change_T) >= EVENT_SAVE_SETTLE_TICKS` (30) conjunct and says Save/Load 'conforms (G1)'. Save/Load owns the function, and its F-1 and registry L3866 have no settle term. Save/Load OQ-41 (L1433, verified) says outright: 'EVENT_SAVE_SETTLE_TICKS ... is not adopted here, because no ruling covers it'. AC-MSA-54 (L1749, verified) asserts 'false at T - last_shape_change_T 29 and true at 30'. That cannot pass against the owner's formula, so whichever GDD the programmer implements from, one AC fails. The worked examples are also 30 ticks apart (437430 / 2570 / 8330 here, 437400 / 2600 / 8360 in Save/Load AC-SL-144). This is the fourth consecutive report. G3 requires carried-over items to land. G1 settles the direction and needs no new decision. The main review held this at RECOMMENDED because the defaults still run. I am promoting it: a contract contradiction between two GDDs with an AC that cannot pass is a real blocker, and the review already said to promote it if this pass did not close it."
 ]
